// 1. At epoch start: $\mu \leftarrow$ compute_full_gradient(); reset $d_0 \leftarrow \mu$; take a step $\eta\,\mu$
// 2. For each minibatch i with current $x_t$, previous $x_{t-1}$:
// 3.   $a_t = \min\!\left(1 - 1/\sqrt{t+1},\, 0.999\right)$
// 4.   $g_t = \nabla f_i(x_t)$,  $g_{t-1}' = \nabla f_i(x_{t-1})$
// 5.   $d_t = (1-a_t)\,g_t + a_t\,(d_{t-1} + g_t - g_{t-1}')$
// 6.   if $\|d_t\| > 3\,\|g_t\|$: rescale $d_t$ to that ratio
// 7.   $\eta_t = \min(\mathrm{lr},\, 0.01\,\|x_t\|/\|d_t\|)$
// 8.   $x_{t+1} = x_t - \eta_t\,d_t$;  $x_{t-1} \leftarrow x_t$

// 1. At epoch start: snapshot $\tilde x \leftarrow x$;  $\mu \leftarrow$ compute_full_gradient($\tilde x$)
// 2. For each minibatch i:
// 3.   $g_t = \nabla f_i(x)$;  evaluate $g_{\text{snap}} = \nabla f_i(\tilde x)$ via param swap
// 4.   $v_t = g_t - g_{\text{snap}} + \mu$
// 5.   if loss = mse: clip $v_t$ to $\|v_t\| \le 5$
// 6.   if loss = cross_entropy: $m \leftarrow 0.9 m + 0.1 v_t$;  update = $m$;  every $n/B$ steps refresh trust scale = clip$(0.01\,\|x\|/\|m\|, 0.1, 5)$
// 7.   else: update = $v_t$, scale = 1
// 8.   $x \leftarrow x - \mathrm{lr}\cdot\text{scale}\cdot$update

// 1. At epoch start: snapshot $\tilde x \leftarrow x$, $\mu \leftarrow$ compute_full_gradient
// 2. For each minibatch i:
// 3.   $g_t = \nabla f_i(x)$,  $g_{\text{snap}} = \nabla f_i(\tilde x)$
// 4.   $v_t = g_t - g_{\text{snap}} + \mu$  (SVRG control variate)
// 5.   $m_i \leftarrow \beta_1 m_i + (1-\beta_1)v_t$,  $v_i \leftarrow \beta_2 v_i + (1-\beta_2) v_t^2$
// 6.   bias-correct $\hat m, \hat v$;  $u_i = \hat m_i/(\sqrt{\hat v_i}+\varepsilon)$
// 7.   global LAMB trust: $\eta_t = \min(\mathrm{lr},\, \|x\| / (\|u\|+\varepsilon))$
// 8.   $x \leftarrow x - \eta_t\,u$

// 1. At epoch start: anchor $x^\sim \leftarrow x$,  $\mu \leftarrow$ compute_full_gradient($x^\sim$);  $d \leftarrow \mu$ if uninitialised
// 2. $\beta = 1 - 1/\sqrt{n/B + 1}$
// 3. For each minibatch i with $x_t, x_{t-1}, x^\sim$:
// 4.   $g_t, g_{t-1}', g_a$ = grads at three points on the same batch
// 5.   $d_{\text{rec}} = \beta\,d + (1-\beta)\,g_t + \beta(g_t - g_{t-1}')$
// 6.   $d_{\text{anc}} = g_t - g_a + \mu$
// 7.   $\mathrm{mix} = \mathrm{clip}\!\left(\|d_{\text{anc}}\| / (\|d_{\text{anc}}\| + \|d_{\text{rec}} - d_{\text{anc}}\|),\, 0.15, 0.85\right)$
// 8.   $d_{\mathrm{blend}} = \mathrm{mix}\,d_{\text{rec}} + (1-\mathrm{mix})\,d_{\text{anc}}$
// 9.   if loss=mse: $\eta_t = \min(\mathrm{lr}, 0.05/\|d\|)$  else $\eta_t = $ lr (with a similar fallback)
// 10. $x \leftarrow x - \eta_t\,d_{\mathrm{blend}}$;  $x_{t-1} \leftarrow x_t$

// 1. First epoch only: $d_0 \leftarrow$ compute_full_gradient(); take one step
// 2. For each minibatch i with $x_t, x_{t-1}$:
// 3.   $g_t, g_{t-1}'$ = grads at $x_t$ and $x_{t-1}$ on the same batch
// 4.   $a_{\text{base}} = \min(1 - 1/\sqrt{t+1},\, 0.999)$  (STORM momentum)
// 5.   $q = |\cos(d_{t-1}, g_t)|$  (alignment quality)
// 6.   $a_t = a_{\text{base}} \cdot (0.8 + 0.2\,q)$  (momentum floor 80 %)
// 7.   $d_t = (1-a_t)\,g_t + a_t\,(d_{t-1} + g_t - g_{t-1}')$
// 8.   if $\|d_t\| > 3\,\|g_t\|$: rescale $d_t$
// 9.   $\eta_t = \min(\mathrm{lr},\, 0.01\,\|x\|/\|d_t\|)$;  $x \leftarrow x - \eta_t d_t$
